+## When `beforeSession` throws
+
+`beforeSession` runs inside the same `try` as the rest of the turn, so a throw from it is handled like any other orchestrator failure (re-cinq/HALEngine#94).
+
+- The throw still reaches the caller as a rejection, and `onError` and `afterSession` both fire for it ([validated by: runs onError and afterSession when beforeSession throws](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.beforeSession.acceptance.test.ts#L40)).
+- `onError` receives the error `beforeSession` threw, the same argument shape as any other failure in the turn ([validated by: hands onError the error a throwing beforeSession raised](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.test.ts#L116)).
+- A hook that runs after a failed `beforeSession` can assume nothing past it happened: no user-input hook ran, no tool ran and the provider was never called ([validated by: never calls the provider when beforeSession throws](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.test.ts#L134)).
+- The engine passes `afterSession` no flag saying the session never started. A hook that allocates in `beforeSession` and releases in `afterSession` must record its own allocation, for example on a `WeakMap` keyed by the session, and release only what it finds there.
+
